<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Duratius</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1st century BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/1st-century-bce">1st century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Duratius was a leader of the Pictones, a Gallic people of the lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/loire">Loire</a> and Poitou, who remained loyal to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rome">Rome</a> during the Gallic revolts against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/julius-caesar">Julius Caesar</a>. In 51 BCE he was besieged in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poitiers">Lemonum</a> (Poitiers) by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dumnacus">Dumnacus</a> of the Andecavi until Roman forces relieved him. Caesar's Gallic War records him as a constant friend of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/roman-empire">Romans</a>.</p></div>
